{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"We recorded GI and STN local field potentials (LFPs) via externalized cables in 38 patients with PD (35 reporting FOG in daily life), both OFF‐ and ON‐dopamine (DOPA).\",\n    \"DOPAOFF, 12 patients with PD had FOG observed (FOG‐OBS, 263 episodes), occurring at a mean of 8 steps after GI, and 26 had no FOG observed (NOBS; FOG‐NOBS).\",\n    \"During the DOPAOFF recording session (1,229 trials), we observed FOG episodes in 12 of these 35 patients with PD during straight‐ahead walking or turning (FOG‐OBS), whereas 23 patients with PD had no FOG episodes (FOG‐NOBS) (Fig 1E‐G).\",\n    \"In the 12 FOG‐OBS patients with PD, we recorded 99 trials where a FOG event occurred in the DOPAOFF condition (FOG‐OBS+ trials), with a median onset of 8 steps (interquartile range [IQR] = 6–11.5) after GI, and a total of 263 FOG episodes (Fig 1E–G).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法 cannot_tell：全文是一篇发表于 Annals of Neurology 的正式论文，没有提及 bioRxiv 预印本，也没有提供预印本与正式发表版本之间的对应关系。因此，仅凭全文无法判断报告 Y 是否将两个版本分别列为证据来源，也无法判断其是否充分标注版本关系及队列重叠；全文没有相关信息，不能据此认定报告读错。指控者的说法 partly：其关于原研究样本量及冻结事件数量的描述有明确依据，全文报告纳入38名帕金森病患者，DOPA-OFF 条件下12名患者观察到冻结，共发生263次冻结事件。但是，全文没有提及 bioRxiv 预印本，也没有说明预印本与正式发表论文是否为同一研究、是否使用完全相同的队列。因此，关于两个版本对应同一研究及同一队列、不应重复计为独立研究的判断，无法由本文全文独立证实。综合而言，指控者引用的核心样本数据正确，但版本关系及队列重叠的判断缺少本文内的直接证据。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "12369e8a-f65f-45a6-a025-1fa093c2930b", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T104929566797Z", "elapsed_seconds": 22.172, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T10:49:51.743690+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disab